    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d708">

                <pb facs="0996" n="986" sameAs="frus:frus1946v10/pg986"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/5–1246: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Davis</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-05-21T15:00:00-04:00">May 21, 1946—3
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>888. As Dept understands proposal in Urtel 827, May 12, additional credit if
                    granted should be on condition that no exchange be allocated for purchase
                    non-American cotton until a further $7 million has been <pb facs="0997" n="987"
                        xml:id="pg987"/> allocated for American cotton thus assuring total American
                    sales of 47 million. Dept believes proposal inappropriate and in conflict with
                    principles American trade program. However, sentiment in Eximbank seems adverse
                    to Chinese request but no action taken.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
